# AINav Control Plane — Cursor project rules
# Company: AINav, Inc. | Public edge: AINav.Institute | Product: AINav Control Plane

## Identity
- Legal entity: **AINav, Inc.**
- Public edge / pin: **AINav.Institute**
- Product name: **AINav Control Plane** (shorthand: AINav)
- Do NOT introduce a second brand (no Aether SKUs, no "Institute product")

## Job (only)
- **Job C — Effect authority:** May this privileged agent *write* run under dual human admit, with DecisionRecords, before the SoR moves?
- Not Job A (agent inventory / shadow-AI / AISPM)
- Not Job B (IdP / Agent 365 / Okta replacement)
- Complement identity and agent security; do not claim to replace them

## Dual admission (non-negotiable)
- Required SoD roles → single-use tokens bound to request_id + action_hash
- Triple hash: token.action_hash == request.action_hash == hash(Action at execute)
- Atomic both-or-neither consume; execute-only burn
- Named principals; distinct humans (no self-approve)
- Fail-closed: partial dual, expiry, revoke, store down, hash mutation → no effect
- Lab single-host atomicity is proven; multi-host HA needs Redis/SQL plane (do not claim HA until wired)

## Commercial
- Land only via FIRST_OFFER L1: $28k / $35k / $40k (band $25–40k)
- Primary attach: P-ADM $40–60k/yr
- U-DUAL never free with connectors
- Fixtures before live SoR; no fail-open discounts
- L1 ≠ ARR

## Code / docs priorities
- Prefer agent-governance/agent_gov for admit plane
- Prefer docs/NAMING.md, docs/BUSINESS_MODEL.md, docs/DUAL_INDEX.md, docs/PRODUCT_BAR_MAXIMUM.md
- Public site source: mothership/www/ (pin/verify culture)
- Run: `cd agent-governance && bash scripts/run_gap_closure_fixtures.sh`

## Language
- Prefer: authority coverage, dual admission, DecisionRecord, fail-closed, hash-bound
- Avoid: gold standard / state of the art / cutting edge unless earned by pin + signed L1
- Never: GENIUS/AI Act "certified" product labels

## Success equation
LIVE_PIN_OK × proof day × signed L1 FIRST_OFFER
